# SDD + TDD Rules

## Non-negotiable order

1. Spec en **`club_management/specs/<feature>.md`** dentro del paquete de la app (p. ej. en este repo: `development/frappe-bench/apps/club_management/club_management/specs/`) usando **Given / When / Then**.
2. Failing test in **`test_<something>.py`** that encodes the spec.
3. Minimum production code (DocType JSON, Python, JS if applicable) to pass.
4. Refactor without breaking tests.

## Never skip

- No production logic in `.py` or `.js` without a failing test that justified it.
- No new fields, DocTypes, or hooks “just in case” without spec + test.

## Where tests live (Frappe)

- Next to the DocType: `apps/club_management/club_management/<module>/doctype/<name>/test_<name>.py`
- Integration / cross-DocType: `apps/club_management/club_management/tests/test_<area>.py`

Use **`FrappeTestCase`** and site DB rollback patterns as in [Frappe automated testing](https://docs.frappe.io/framework/user/en/guides/automated-testing) guidance.
